cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use axionFEM, please cite it using the metadata in this file, and also cite
  J. N. Benabou, J. W. Foster, B. R. Safdi, to appear (2026).
  Please also cite the papers whose methods or benchmarks you rely on, and MFEM.
type: software
title: axionFEM
abstract: >-
  axionFEM is a finite-element package for designing and evaluating axion dark-matter
  detectors. It covers lumped-element detectors from the field solve to the scan reach
  (magnetoquasistatics, full wave, readout circuits, mechanics and heat conduction,
  optimization). Cavity haloscopes, SRF heterodyne cavities, dc SQUID readout chains,
  incompressible flow and electrochemistry are beta modules. A C++17 core built on MFEM
  performs the solves; a Python API, a command line, an interactive 3D viewer and an MCP
  server for AI assistants sit on top.
authors:
  - given-names: Joshua N.
    family-names: Benabou
  - given-names: Joshua W.
    family-names: Foster
  - given-names: Benjamin R.
    family-names: Safdi
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-09
license: BSD-3-Clause
repository-code: https://github.com/bsafdi/axionFEM
url: https://bsafdi.github.io/axionFEM/
keywords:
  - axion
  - dark matter
  - finite element
  - electromagnetics
  - haloscope
  - lumped-element detector
  - MFEM
